function COMPONENT(request : dval) {
    print("<div class=\"doc-detail-layout\"><main class=\"content doc-page doc-detail\"><h2>RENDER</h2><div class=\"doc-section signatures\"><h3>Capy</h3><pre>function RENDER(request : dval)\nfunction RENDER:NAME(request : dval)</pre></div><div class=\"doc-section content\"><p><code>RENDER</code> is the HTTP entrypoint of a unit. When a request routes to a <code>.capy</code> file, Bearer calls that file&#39;s <code>RENDER</code> handler.</p><p>The handler takes one parameter, <code>request</code>, of type <code>dval</code>, and returns nothing. Everything it <code>print</code>s becomes the response body.</p><h2>A minimal page</h2><p>function RENDER(request : dval) {\n    print(&quot;&lt;h1&gt;Hello&lt;/h1&gt;&quot;)\n}</p><p>Read input from the request snapshot with a converter and a fallback, so a missing parameter has a defined value:</p><p>var name := string(request.query.name, &quot;guest&quot;)</p><h2>Response control</h2><p><code>print()</code> writes the body. Set status, headers, and cookies in <code>request.out</code>:</p><p>request.out.status = 404\nrequest.out.headers[&quot;Cache-Control&quot;] = &quot;no-store&quot;\nrequest.out.cookies[&quot;visited&quot;] = &quot;1&quot;</p><p><code>redirect()</code> sets the status and <code>Location</code> header together. A handler may <code>return</code> early at any point; whatever it printed so far is still sent.</p><h2>Named handlers</h2><p><code>RENDER:NAME</code> declares an additional named entrypoint in the same file, selected by the caller rather than by the URL path. A file&#39;s unnamed <code>RENDER</code> remains the one that plain routing reaches.</p><h2>What runs around it</h2><p>The unit&#39;s <code>ONCE</code> handler runs before <code>RENDER</code> the first time the unit is used in a request. Fragments are pulled in with <cod")
    print("e>component_render()</code> or <code>component()</code>; another unit&#39;s exported functions are reached with <code>unit_load()</code> or <code>unit_call()</code>.</p><p>Every Capy unit must export at least one handler — <code>RENDER</code>, <code>CLI</code>, <code>COMPONENT</code>, <code>WS</code>, <code>ONCE</code>, or <code>INIT</code> — or metadata via <code>#exports</code>. A file with none fails to compile.</p></div><div class=\"doc-section example\"><h3>Example</h3><div class=\"example-language capy\"><h4>Capy</h4><pre class=\"example-source\">print(string(request.method, &quot;&quot;), &quot;\\n&quot;)\n</pre></div></div><div class=\"doc-section example\"><h3>Example</h3><div class=\"example-language capy\"><h4>Capy</h4><pre class=\"example-source\">print(&quot;&lt;h1&gt;Hello, &quot;, string(request.query.name, &quot;guest&quot;), &quot;&lt;/h1&gt;&quot;, &quot;\\n&quot;)\n</pre></div></div><div class=\"doc-section example\"><h3>Example</h3><div class=\"example-language capy\"><h4>Capy</h4><pre class=\"example-source\">request.out.status = 201\nrequest.out.headers[&quot;X-Demo&quot;] = &quot;yes&quot;\nprint(&quot;created\\n&quot;)\n</pre></div></div><div class=\"doc-section example\"><h3>Example</h3><div class=\"example-language capy\"><h4>Capy</h4><pre class=\"example-source\">if !request.query.id? {\n    request.out.status = 400\n    print(&quot;id required\\n&quot;)\n    return\n}\nprint(&quot;id &quot;, s64(request.query.id, 0), &quot;\\n&quot;)\n</pre></div></div></main><aside class=\"doc-section see-also\"><h3>See also</h3><a class=\"related-link\" href=\"/doc/type/request/\">request</a><a class=\"related-link\" href=\"/doc/handler/component/\">component</a><a class=\"related-link\" href=\"/doc/handler/cli/\">cli</a><a class=\"related-link\" href=\"/doc/handler/ws/\">ws</a><a class=\"related-link\" href=\"/doc/a")
    print("pi/component/\">component</a><a class=\"related-link\" href=\"/doc/api/redirect/\">redirect</a></aside></div>")
}
